# PDFs are binary. Git's own text/binary heuristic only looks for a NUL
# byte in the first few KB of a file - a small hand-built PDF (see
# fixtures/synthetic/pdfs/*.pdf) can easily have none, so without this
# rule Git treats it as text and rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout wherever
# core.autocrlf=true (the common Windows default, and the default this
# repo's local dev machines actually run with). That silently corrupts a
# PDF's byte-exact xref offsets and content-stream /Length values -
# confirmed by forcing a checkout of an unmarked fixture and watching its
# byte length change. `-text` disables any EOL translation for the match,
# regardless of what the content-sniffing heuristic would have guessed.
*.pdf -text
